WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.004 --> 00:00:07.751
Migration shows whether your records would load into the new system, and what to fix first.

2
00:00:07.751 --> 00:00:13.002
The banner gives the current verdict from the latest analysis.

3
00:00:13.002 --> 00:00:19.996
Workbook from the new system: fill the new system's own workbook or load file from a finished run.

4
00:00:19.996 --> 00:00:25.342
Three steps: choose the run and workbook, check what fits, export the data.

5
00:00:25.342 --> 00:00:31.200
Choose the workbook or load file the new system gave you.

6
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:38.175
Check the workbook reads it. The workbook itself is not kept and nothing is exported yet.

7
00:00:38.175 --> 00:00:44.827
How many rows are ready, how many are held back, and how many sheets can be filled.

8
00:00:44.827 --> 00:00:50.489
Required columns with no data are named, because the new system refuses those rows.

9
00:00:50.489 --> 00:00:58.135
Columns the workbook asks for that the extraction did not fetch are added to the extraction, so Meridian learns them.

10
00:00:58.135 --> 00:01:05.103
Update the run starts a new extraction that fetches the added columns from the source system.

11
00:01:05.103 --> 00:01:10.441
When the new run finishes, choose it above and check the workbook again.

12
00:01:10.441 --> 00:01:16.453
Then export in the same format, as Excel, or as CSV files, ready to load.

13
00:01:16.453 --> 00:01:22.121
Gaps by kind: why records would not load, grouped by the kind of problem.
